 "fylite:executable": false,
 "fylite:executable_note": "Not callable in this distribution since 2026-09-07: the entry is the `input.tglf` DECK face (`scenario.model:tglf` over `gyrofluid.py`), and a deck is an external serialisation format — the kernel is forbidden to parse one, so the face could not sink into a door. It had no caller in this package, its tests or the app; every consumer was a port-validation test, so both the face and its reference reader moved to the kernel repository (`tests/oracles/gyrofluid.py`) and neither `scenario.model.tglf` nor the MCP tool `fylite_tglf` exists here any more. THE PHYSICS IS STILL SHIPPED: the TGLF port runs in the extension binary and is reached through its own door — `fydoc.complete(\"code/turbulence\", …)`, a transport profile in and chi out, which is also what `scenario.model.evolve(closure=\"turbulent\")` marches on. What is no longer offered is the deck-shaped question (eigenvalues / flux spectrum for a given input.tglf)."
}
